The change replaces `push_back(Field(...))` with `emplace_back(...)`. This constructs the new `Field` directly in the vector's storage, avoiding a temporary and a copy or move. The lookup and return behaviour are unchanged. `fields.back()` is the same element that `fields[fields.size() - 1]` referred to.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::AddField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    Field *field = GetField(fieldNum);

    if (field == FIT_NULL)
    {
        fields.emplace_back(profile->num, fieldNum);
        field = &fields.back();
    }

    return field;
}
```

